# Local-first → promote to this repo

## Order of work

1. Build/try the feature in the **private local runner** (`../anima-lora-batch/` or equivalent), not here first.
2. Confirm it works (skip/download/retry, SM sidecars, etc.).
3. **Carry over** a scrubbed, generalized version into this `civitmatrix/` tree.
4. Re-test the public copy, then commit and push to `ArturoWolff/civitmatrix`.

## Hard rules

- Never commit secrets, personal absolute paths, `.env`, logs, or weights.
- Prefer promoting stable behavior over half-finished experiments.
- Docs-only or explicit “do it in civitmatrix” requests are the exception.
- UI work still follows the Win95 browser rule once promoted here.

## Checklist before push

- [ ] Proven locally  
- [ ] No private paths/keys in the diff  
- [ ] CLI/env stays portable (Linux/macOS/Windows)  
- [ ] Smoke-tested from this folder (`python -m civitmatrix --help` / dry-run as relevant)
